"url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For a single value, prefer a visible `label`; use `aria-label` only when equivalent visible context already exists."},"1044":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For an array, provide one descriptive `thumbLabels` entry for every value. Entries are matched by index, so keep them aligned when values are added, removed, or reordered. Describe each thumb's purpose, such as `Lower warning threshold`, rather than its current number."},"1045":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."},"1046":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-41","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Each thumb follows the React Aria slider keyboard model:"},"1047":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-42","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Tab and Shift+Tab move among thumbs and surrounding controls."},"1048":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-43","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Right and Arrow Up increase the focused value by `step`."},"1049":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-44","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Left and Arrow Down decrease the focused value by `step`."},"1050":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-45","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Home and End move the focused thumb to its permitted bounds."},"1051":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-46","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Page Up and Page Down make larger changes."},"1052":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-47","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Directional behavior follows the user's locale where appropriate. Pointer, touch, and keyboard interaction all use the same scale and constraints."},"1053":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-48","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Markers are decorative and hidden from the accessibility tree. Ensure the field label, thumb labels, bounds, step, and formatted values communicate all required information without relying on marker appearance."},"1054":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-49","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use an array only when every entry has a clear, independently adjustable meaning."},"1055":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-50","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep `value`, `thumbLabels`, and `thumbNames` aligned by index."},"1056":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-51","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use thumb labels that explain purpose instead of repeating the current number."},"1057":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-52","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep array values in a stable semantic order. If crossing or reordering thumbs would make their meaning ambiguous, enforce the appropriate ordering in product state."},"1058":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-53","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Avoid large value arrays. Every entry creates another focusable control, which increases keyboard effort and cognitive load."},"1059":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-54","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Set meaningful `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` values. The scale should match the precision users actually need."},"1060":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-55","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use markers only when there are few enough steps to scan. Tiny steps across a large range can create an excessive number of DOM elements."},"1061":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-56","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `formatOptions` for currency, percentages, measurements, and other locale-sensitive units so values display and announce their meaning."},"1062":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-57","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `description` for persistent guidance and `isRequired` when a value is required."},"1063":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-58","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value should remain visible but unavailable for interaction."},"1064":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-59","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `onChange` for lightweight immediate feedback and `onChangeEnd` for expensive requests, filtering, or calculations."},"1065":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-60","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use a text-entry control when exact numeric input is essential. A track is best for exploring or adjusting values within known bounds."},"1066":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-61","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"Check the same index in `thumbLabels` and `thumbNames`. Each array entry renders a thumb, and its accessible label and form name are read from the corresponding positions. A form name does not replace an accessible label."},"1067":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-62","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"Keep the controlled or default value and callback signatures consistent. When inference is unavailable, provide the generic explicitly: `<RangeField<number>>` for a scalar or `<RangeField<number[]>>` for an array."},"1068":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-63","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The `value` prop is the source of truth. Update the scalar or array in `onChange` without changing its intended shape. For arrays, return a new array so application state observes the update."},"1069":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-64","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Verify that `step` represents the intended interval from `minValue`. Every thumb snaps to valid positions on the same configured scale."},"1070":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-65","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"Markers begin at `minValue` and appear at complete step positions. `maxValue` receives a marker only when the range is evenly divisible by `step`."},"1071":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-66","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Increase `step` or omit `markers`. Large ranges with small steps can produce many decorative elements even when users cannot distinguish them visually."},"1072":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-67","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"Enable automatic current-value output with `valueLabel={true}` or provide custom content. `minLabel` and `maxLabel` display only explicitly supplied content; neither defaults to a numeric bound or receives `formatOptions`."},"1073":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-68","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values are supported. Set a negative `minValue` and ensure every scalar or array value remains within the configured bounds."},"1074":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-69","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"Provide finite bounds where `minValue` is less than `maxValue`, a finite `step` greater than zero, and finite values inside the configured range."},"1075":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"page","content":"SegmentedController","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller"},"1076":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-0","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","content":"A segmented controller is a linear set of two or more segments, each of which functions as a button. A segmented controller allows users to select options, switch views, or sort elements."},"1077":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-1","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#installation","content":"Installation"},"1078":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-2","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#examples","content":"Examples"},"1079":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-3","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#default","content":"Default"},"1080":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-4","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1081":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-5","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1082":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-6","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon--text","content":"Icon + Text"},"1083":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-7","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon-only","content":"Icon Only"},"1084":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-8","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#overflow","content":"Overflow"},"1085":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-9","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#rtl-direction","content":"RTL Direction"},"1086":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-10","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#disabled-states","content":"Disabled States"},"1087":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-11","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#customization","content":"Customization"},"1088":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-12","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"Data Attributes"},"1089":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-13","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1090":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-14","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"Keyboard Navigation"},"1091":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-15","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"1092":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-16","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1093":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-17","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When to Use a Segmented Controller"},"1094":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-18","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-not-to-use","content":"When Not to Use"},"1095":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-19","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#props","content":"Props"},"1096":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-20","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#segmentedcontroller","content":"SegmentedController"},"1097":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-21","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#segmentedcontrolleritem","content":"SegmentedControllerItem"},"1098":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-22","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#default","content":"An uncontrolled segmented controller with a default selection. The component manages its own state internally via `defaultValue`."},"1099":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-23","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#controlled","content":"Use `value` and `onSelectionChange` to fully control the selected segment from parent state."},"1100":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-24","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#sizes","content":"Three sizes are available: `sm`, `md` (default), and `lg`."},"1101":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-25","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon--text","content":"Segments can include an `Icon` alongside text for added visual context."},"1102":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-26","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon-only","content":"For compact layouts, segments can contain only icons. Provide an `aria-label` on each item so screen readers can identify the action."},"1103":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-27","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#overflow","content":"When the number of options exceeds the width of the container, the component automatically shows scroll buttons to let users navigate. Users can also scroll horizontally to navigate the options."},"1104":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-28","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#rtl-direction","content":"The segmented controller follows the current layout direction (LTR or RTL), detected automatically from the browser or system settings."},"1105":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-29","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#disabled-states","content":"Disable the entire group with `isDisabled` on the container, or disable individual segments with `isDisabled` on specific items."},"1106":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-30","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"Components automatically add data attributes for styling different states:"},"1107":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-31","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"**SegmentedController Container:** `data-disabled`"},"1108":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-32","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"**SegmentedControllerItem:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"},"1109":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-33","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the segmented controller"},"1110":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-34","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Arrow Left/Right**: Move to next/previous segment"},"1111":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-35","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Space/Enter**: Select the focused segment"},"1112":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-36","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"},"1113":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-37","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"},"1114":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-38","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"},"1115":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-39","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"},"1116":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-40","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"},"1117":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-41","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When switching between 2-5 related views within the same context"},"1118":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-42","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When all options should be visible at once"},"1119":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-43","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When the selection immediately changes the displayed content"},"1120":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-44","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-not-to-use","content":"For more than 5 options (use Tabs or Select instead)"},"1121":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-45","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-not-to-use","content":"For form input (use RadioGroup instead)"},"1122":{"id":"/docs/components/select","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"page","content":"Select","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select"},"1123":{"id":"/docs/components/select-0","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select","content":"Select is a dropdown for picking one or more values from a list of options. It renders a labeled trigger and a popover listbox, supports single and multiple selection, and submits naturally inside a form."},"1124":{"id":"/docs/components/select-1","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"Features"},"1125":{"id":"/docs/components/select-2","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#installation","content":"Installation"},"1126":{"id":"/docs/components/select-3","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#examples","content":"Examples"},"1127":{"id":"/docs/components/select-4","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#default","content":"Default"},"1128":{"id":"/docs/components/select-5","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1129":{"id":"/docs/components/select-6","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#multiple","content":"Multiple"},"1130":{"id":"/docs/components/select-7","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#invalid","content":"Invalid"},"1131":{"id":"/docs/components/select-8","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"1132":{"id":"/docs/components/select-9","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#form","content":"Form"},"1133":{"id":"/docs/components/select-10","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1134":{"id":"/docs/components/select-11","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#composed","content":"Composed"},"1135":{"id":"/docs/components/select-12","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#props","content":"Props"},"1136":{"id":"/docs/components/select-13","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#select","content":"Select"},"1137":{"id":"/docs/components/select-14","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectoptions","content":"SelectOptions"},"1138":{"id":"/docs/components/select-15","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectvalue","content":"SelectValue"},"1139":{"id":"/docs/components/select-16","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectitem","content":"SelectItem"},"1140":{"id":"/docs/components/select-17","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, a `Button slot=\"trigger\"`, `SelectOptions`, and optional `Text` / `FieldError`. Nothing is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in"},"1141":{"id":"/docs/components/select-18","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"},"1142":{"id":"/docs/components/select-19","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Composed in another field**: Use `variant=\"control\"` to sit inside another field's `Group`, as a country-code select beside a phone `Input`"},"1143":{"id":"/docs/components/select-20","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values"},"1144":{"id":"/docs/components/select-21","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state, or `defaultValue` for uncontrolled"},"1145":{"id":"/docs/components/select-22","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"},"1146":{"id":"/docs/components/select-23","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Form integration**: Set `name` and the value submits as part of a native `<form>` (multiple values submit as repeated entries)"},"1147":{"id":"/docs/components/select-24","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**React Aria integration**: Built on React Aria Select for accessibility, keyboard navigation, and typeahead"},"1148":{"id":"/docs/components/select-25","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#default","content":"Minimal usage with a `Label`, items, and a placeholder."},"1149":{"id":"/docs/components/select-26